      <div class="legal-section" id="en" data-lang-section="en">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: November 23, 2026 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Version 1.3</p>

        <div class="legal-notice">
          <p>This Privacy Policy describes how FamlyBudget collects, uses, and protects the personal data of users of the FamlyBudget app for Android and iOS and of its web version, used from a browser with the same account.</p>
        </div>

        <h2>1. Data Controller</h2>
        <p>The Data Controller for personal data is:</p>
        <p><strong>Fabrizio Ganem</strong><br />
        Email: <a href="mailto:privacy@famlybudget.com">privacy@famlybudget.com</a><br />
        Support: <a href="mailto:support@famlybudget.com">support@famlybudget.com</a></p>

        <h2>2. Data Collected</h2>

        <h3>2.1 Account Data</h3>
        <p>To use FamlyBudget you need to authenticate. We collect:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Email address</strong> — provided at registration, via Google Sign-In or via Sign in with Apple (in which case it may be the private relay address generated by Apple)</li>
          <li><strong>Display name</strong> — optional, provided by the user or by the Google or Apple profile</li>
          <li><strong>User identifier (UID)</strong> — generated by Firebase Auth</li>
          <li><strong>Service profile</strong> — a record linked to your account containing: email and name, the storage mode you chose (Local or Cloud), the version and date on which you accepted the Terms and this policy, a code for the active session in the app and one for the web version (used to keep a single sign-in at a time on each), the family you belong to, the app version and the date you last used it on each platform (Android, iOS, web), and the creation and update dates. <strong>This profile stays in the cloud in Local mode too.</strong></li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.2 Financial Data</h3>
        <p>FamlyBudget allows you to choose where to store your data:</p>
        <table>
          <tr><th>Mode</th><th>Where data is saved</th><th>Remote access</th></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Local</strong></td><td>Only on the user's device, in an encrypted database</td><td>No — financial data never leaves the device. Only the account and the service profile (§2.1) stay in the cloud.</td></tr>
          <tr><td><strong>Cloud (Firebase)</strong></td><td>Firebase Firestore (Google Cloud)</td><td>Yes — multi-device sync</td></tr>
        </table>
        <p>Financial data includes: transactions, accounts, categories, budgets, savings goals, recurring entries, and balances. This data is exclusively owned by the user.</p>

        <h3>2.3 Family and people</h3>
        <p>In Cloud mode you can create a family and invite other people. Whoever creates the family is its <strong>owner</strong>: they enter the email address of the people they invite and can add people identified only by a name (for example their children), to assign expenses. Please do not enter any other data about the people you add.</p>
        <p>The data shared in a family (transactions with attached photos and locations, voice drafts, shared lists, people) <strong>belongs to the family and is managed by the owner</strong>: invited members enter and edit it on the owner's behalf, within the role the owner gives them. All members can see the family's data.</p>
        <p>If an invited member deletes their account, the data they entered in the family <strong>stays with the family</strong>: to have it erased they can ask the owner, who can delete it from the app (partial or full reset). The app does not delete it automatically.</p>

        <h3>2.4 Optional data attached to transactions</h3>
        <p>When you record an expense or income you can choose to attach:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Your location.</strong> Only if you tap the button to add a location, the app asks for permission to access the device's precise location and saves latitude and longitude with that single transaction. The app does not detect your location at any other time, nor in the background. You can remove it from the transaction or revoke the permission in the device settings at any time. The location map only loads when you tap "Show map" or pick the point on the map (see §4).</li>
          <li><strong>A photo of a receipt</strong>, taken with the camera or chosen from the gallery. The app does not read other photos on your device. Before saving it, the app removes the hidden data that the camera and gallery add to the file (such as the GPS location where it was taken, the date and the phone model); only the orientation is kept, so the photo displays upright. You can remove it from the transaction at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>In Local mode this data stays on your device only. In Cloud mode it is saved on Firestore together with the transaction and, if you share your data with a family, it is visible to the other members.</p>

        <h3>2.5 Voice entry (optional)</h3>
        <p>You can dictate an expense or income by voice (for example "I spent 12 euros at the bar"). The feature only starts if you tap the microphone button and only if you grant the microphone and speech recognition permissions, which you can revoke at any time in the device settings.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Microphone.</strong> The app listens only while the listening screen is open, for a maximum of 30 seconds per phrase. It does not listen in the background.</li>
          <li><strong>Speech recognition.</strong> Turning your voice into text is done by the speech recognition service of the device's operating system (Google on Android, Apple on iOS), not by FamlyBudget. Depending on the device, the language and the settings, the audio may be processed on the device or sent to the provider's servers, which handles it under its own privacy policy. FamlyBudget cannot guarantee that the audio stays on the device.</li>
          <li><strong>Audio.</strong> The app does not record, save or send the audio to our servers: it only receives the recognized text from the system.</li>
          <li><strong>Text of the phrase.</strong> The recognized text is used to work out amount, type, account, category and date. If you do not confirm the transaction right away, the phrase stays saved in the voice draft until you confirm or delete it; at that point the draft is deleted. In Local mode the draft stays on your device only. In Cloud mode it is saved on Firestore with your other data and, if you share your data with a family, it is visible to the other members. The confirmed transaction keeps only a marker that it was entered by voice, not the phrase.</li>
          <li><strong>Learned habits.</strong> To understand your phrases better, the app remembers some of your choices locally (for example which account you mean with a certain word). These rules stay <strong>on the device only</strong>, are not synced or included in backups, and you can view, delete or export them as a CSV file from the "Learned habits" screen. The exported file contains the words you used and is kept by you: the app does not send it anywhere.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>2.6 Technical and Diagnostic Data</h3>
        <p>We automatically collect technical data to find and fix errors in the app:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Firebase Crashlytics</strong> — crash reports and technical anomalies. Each report contains technical information (app version, device model and operating system, error details) and is associated with the Firebase user identifier (UID), a random code that does not contain your email or name, and with the storage mode in use (Local or Cloud). Reports do not contain your financial data.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>The app does not use usage-behavior analytics or advertising tools.</p>

        <h3>2.7 Web version</h3>
        <p>If you use FamlyBudget from a browser:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Anti-abuse check.</strong> Each time it opens, the web version loads Google reCAPTCHA Enterprise, which Firebase App Check uses to verify that requests come from the genuine app. Google receives the IP address and technical information about the browser and device, and may set its own technical cookie.</li>
          <li><strong>Data in the browser.</strong> To open faster, the web version keeps in the browser a copy of the data you view, along with your sign-in session and some preferences. If you tick "Shared or public computer" when signing in, the sign-in ends when you close the tab and your data is kept in memory only: no copy stays in the browser, and copies left by earlier sign-ins are erased. You can also use a private browser window, which erases everything when you close it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Purposes of Processing</h2>
        <p>We use the collected data for the following purposes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Service delivery</strong> — authentication, saving and syncing user data</li>
          <li><strong>Diagnostics and stability</strong> — bug detection and resolution via Crashlytics</li>
          <li><strong>Voice entry</strong> — turning the dictated phrase into a draft transaction, at your request</li>
          <li><strong>Service communications</strong> — emails for essential communications (for example substantial changes to this policy)</li>
          <li><strong>Security</strong> — verifying that requests come from the genuine app (Firebase App Check) and keeping a single sign-in at a time</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not use data for third-party advertising, commercial profiling, or sale to third parties.</p>

